    {
      "id": "474b7ef4d3504b5c",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1622,
      "y": 1000,
      "width": 736,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "an",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1474501083,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 769794846,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784146805901,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHY THIS DESIGN\n\nExisting APIs stay source of truth\nLLM interprets; it does not invent metrics\nDeterministic detection is reproducible\nTyped tools reduce hallucinated calls\nTemporal-style workflow survives failures\nSSE fits server→client progress streaming\nPostgreSQL provides transactional state\nKafka supports replay and decoupling\nOpenSearch handles entity/runbook retrieval\nOpenTelemetry supports end-to-end diagnosis",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WHY THIS DESIGN\n\nExisting APIs stay source of truth\nLLM interprets; it does not invent metrics\nDeterministic detection is reproducible\nTyped tools reduce hallucinated calls\nTemporal-style workflow survives failures\nSSE fits server→client progress streaming\nPostgreSQL provides transactional state\nKafka supports replay and decoupling\nOpenSearch handles entity/runbook retrieval\nOpenTelemetry supports end-to-end diagnosis",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
